{"query":"Search regulatory or public-health agency primary assessments (FDA, EMA, WHO guideline panels) that independently evaluated ivermectin as a COVID-19 treatment.","results":[{"date":"Aug 31, 2021","position":1,"site_name":"www.fda.gov","snippet":"Sklice is a single-use lotion with ivermectin 0.5% as the active ingredient, for the topical … to be safe or effective for the treatment or prevention of COVID -19 and they are not FDA-approved ...","title":"Search | FDA","url":"https://www.fda.gov/search?s=ivermectin+for+covid"},{"date":"Mar 22, 2021","position":2,"site_name":"www.ema.europa.eu","snippet":"EMA therefore concluded that use of ivermectin for prevention or treatment of COVID-19 cannot currently be recommended outside controlled clinical trials. Further well-designed, randomised studies are needed to draw conclusions as to whether the product is effective and safe in the prevention and treatment of COVID-19.","title":"EMA advises against use of ivermectin for the prevention or ...","url":"https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/news/ema-advises-against-use-ivermectin-prevention-or-treatment-covid-19-outside-randomised-clinical-trials"},{"position":3,"site_name":"www.fda.gov","snippet":"The FDA has not authorized or approved ivermectin for use in preventing or treating COVID-19 in humans or animals.","title":"Ivermectin and COVID-19 | FDA","url":"https://www.fda.gov/consumers/consumer-updates/ivermectin-and-covid-19"},{"date":"Oct 3, 2026","position":4,"site_name":"biologyinsights.com","snippet":"Every major, well-designed randomized trial of ivermectin for COVID-19 has reached the same conclusion: the drug does not produce a clinically meaningful benefit for outpatients with mild to moderate disease. That verdict comes from thousands of participants across multiple countries, tested in blinded, placebo-controlled settings, and confirmed by the most authoritative systematic review on ...","title":"Ivermectin COVID Studies: A Review of Major Trials","url":"https://biologyinsights.com/ivermectin-covid-studies-a-review-of-major-trials/"},{"date":"Aug 23, 2026","position":5,"site_name":"factually.co","snippet":"Major public-health organizations have examined dozens of ivermectin trials and — while some meta-analyses and advocacy groups report large benefits — authoritative bodies such as the World Health Organization and the U.S. COVID-19 Treatment Guidelines Panel concluded evidence is insufficient to recommend ivermectin outside clinical trials ...","title":"How Have Public‑Health Organizations Assessed Ivermectin ...","url":"https://factually.co/fact-checks/health/ivermectin-covid-19-trials-assessments-by-public-health-organizations-4ab226"},{"date":"Feb 25, 2026","position":6,"site_name":"factually.co","snippet":"Regulatory agencies — including the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA), the European Medicines Agency (EMA), and the World Health Organization (WHO) — have reviewed clinical trials and concluded that current evidence does not support using ivermectin to prevent or treat COVID-19 outside of well‑designed clinical trials [1] [2] [3].","title":"What do regulatory agencies (FDA, EMA, WHO) and clinic...","url":"https://factually.co/fact-checks/health/ivermectin-safety-off-label-fda-ema-who-clinical-trials-9f00fe"},{"date":"Apr 5, 2024","position":7,"site_name":"pharmacologypro.com","snippet":"Ivermectin is not FDA-authorized for COVID-19. As of 04/05/2024 the agency has not determined it safe or effective for that use. ACTIV-6 and early-treatment trials did not support outpatient benefit.","title":"Ivermectin for COVID: FDA Status and What Trials Showed","url":"https://pharmacologypro.com/articles/ivermectin-covid-myths/"}],"total_results":7,"page":0}